=== MN l.140-146
**The actor convention.** The proposals queue never sees a fake settlement: `targetSaveId` is always the ANCHOR settlement (a real campaign id — the `where` dial's first id, or derived from the record at mint and re-read at approval against the then-current world); the menace id rides the `subject` composite and is split at stage time (`splitCourseTarget`'s sibling). Every hearing's parties use the one actor-ref convention `{ kind, id? }` with `kind ∈ settlement · person · party · menace · corps · body` — SIX kinds, `bodyKind` (`conclave · gang · beast`) a field of THE BODIES' ref, never a seventh kind [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — RULINGS-ROUND4 A.12 · RULINGS-ROUND3 §G.3 (amending round 3's five): a body decides its own week (`DESIGN_FP_ARCH_BD.md` §2.1, OD-BD-3), so by A.7's own test it is an actor; a MENACE is still the DM's — a body becomes one only by the DM's `PROMOTE_BODY` (§2 below) or by joining a menace whose authored course `enlists` (§6)] (`strategicPosture.js :: POSTURE_ACTOR_KINDS` is `['settlement']` today; widening it is an SP-4a amendment — the chair's fold row, RULINGS-AFTER-RESEARCH §4). A menace has no mind (MN6) and is still an ACTOR, where a site is not: the DM's authored COURSE stands in for its choosing (MN1, MN12 — it goes where the course sends it and nowhere else, so it is a party that acts on the card), while a site has no course and no choice and is a WHERE and a subject only; a corps (`u:`) decides for itself (CH §16b). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — RULINGS-ROUND3 A.7 · the fold verifier's note ("the r2b actor-kind rationale ('posture-bearing DECIDERS; a site has no mind') applies equally to `menace` … which the convention keeps"): the list was four kinds and gave no reason a mindless menace stays one; the fold §1 bracket, the spine mirror and §3.3's row are the chair's at P4.]

**Stage, then approve.** Every realm verb reaches apply as a proposal (`applyMode: 'proposal'`, `forced: true`, `provenance: 'dm'`); AUTHOR's "it is so" is that approval, the landed shape of every AUTHOR act, recorded. **Undo** is the proposal ring's snapshot restore (`campaignWorldPulseSlice.js`); the record and its driven stressors live in one world and restore together. The inverse acts (lower a band, rouse, move back) are DM acts that write history, never undo. [CURED 2026-10-17 (fp-final) — SMN-31.]

**The promotion from a body — `PROMOTE_BODY` hands its dials to `RAISE_MENACE`.** [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — L-BD's route (2) · RULINGS-ROUND4 B (MN): "`RAISE_MENACE` takes the `PROMOTE_BODY` handoff" (`DESIGN_FP_ARCH_BD.md` BD16, §11: "hands the body's place, might and the DM's name to MN's `RAISE_MENACE` … and ends the body `raised`").] THE BODIES' verb `PROMOTE_BODY` (dials: the body · the menace's name · its course; AUTHOR) stages ONE `RAISE_MENACE` proposal in the same act, its four dials filled from the body: `name` = the DM's name (quoted, never parsed — MN2; a body's own derived place-and-kind name is never carried, because BD derives it and the DM names the menace); `where` = the body's place in MN's WHERE words — the country of the settlement its held site is attached to (the attachment's anchor, `where.ids[0]`), or the country it stands in, or the road `a␟b` it holds — never a hidden way (a trail is no MN place; BD names the node country it comes out at); `might` = the body's might key (the same `STRENGTH_BAND_KEYS` ladder BD reads, so no re-banding); `posture` = the verb's course where it is `stays` or `besieges` (with `besieges`, the anchor is the town besieged), and any other course (`toward`, `wanders`, `enlists`) a `MENACE_COURSE` row staged in the same act. The raise then runs exactly as any raise: the ambient raider record in that country is ADOPTED in place (MN12), the id derives from that `RAISE_MENACE` outcome id, and `raisedBy` keeps it — the raise receipt's `causedBy` names the `PROMOTE_BODY` act, so the cause walk reaches the body's own birthplace receipt with no new field on the menace record. What the body leaves behind is the other owners': BD's writer ends the body `raised`, and its row in the presence composer stops the same tick the menace's own rows start (one term per thing); a site the body held passes to the menace through ST's one writer (holder ref `{ kind: 'body', … }` → `{ kind: 'menace', id }`, routed to ST), so the den becomes the menace's lair in prose (MN14). The menace is still the DM's alone: the engine never promotes (BD16; MN12), and approval is the DM's like every AUTHOR act. DARK until THE BODIES lands AND the owner answers OD-BD-6 (THE PROMOTION VERB is the owner's row; the chair recommends yes) — until then a DM who wants a body's gang as a menace raises one by hand where it stands.

**The stressor doors on a held record.** The party-impact doors on a stressor (`resolve_stressor · ease_stressor · worsen_stressor · name_attacker`, `partyImpactKinds.js`) refuse a menace-held record with a receipt that points to the menace's own verbs ("this crisis is the Ashen Host's; move or end the menace to lift it") — one fact, one door; it also keeps a settlement attacker from ever being stamped on a menace record (§3.2). The two DM-authoring doors that pick a world stressor BY TYPE at a town — `store/campaignRegionalSlice.js` (the `resolve` act, "Resolved by DM authoring", and the undo arms `withdraw` and `restore`) and `events/drainQueuedEvents.js :: applyTwinDirectivesToWorld` (`resolve`, "Resolved by DM authoring (queued)") — SKIP a menace-held record in their matcher (`menaceHolds`); where the held record is the only match, the door returns a typed refusal `{ refused: 'menace_held', menaceId }` and the Edit surface offers that menace's `MENACE_STATE` card instead, so the DM's intent reaches the menace and is never silently undone by the next press. The census is closed: those six doors are every world-stressor writer that can select a held record (`cure/D-MN-r1.md` §1(g); the settlement-local `adjustStressorSeverityById` callers in `commonsVoiceKernel.js` and `assizeKernel.js` never touch the world list). [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r1) — MN-r1-9. REFINED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r1) — the typed refusal and its offer of the menace's own card, so a refused act is never a silent no-op.] [REFINED 2026-10-17 (fp-final) — the measurement made the two sponsor-reader guards unneeded (a fresh record is skipped by construction); the guarantee they bought is kept by this door and a pin.] A party's deed against a menace is executed through the menace's own verbs with their `party` dial on (`MENACE_MIGHT` lowering the might → THE PARTY's `party_event` kind `menace_weakened`; `MENACE_STATE end` → `menace_ended`, `DESIGN_FP_ARCH_PT.md` §2.4): the apply arm calls PT's `party_event` door, which mints the deed in RN's deed ledger (`spatialLedgers.deeds` through `deedLedger.js :: mintDeed` — RN owns it, RULINGS-AFTER-COMPILE) when THE PARTY and THE RENOWN are lit; dark, the dial is refused with its reason. A siege the party broke is the DM's verdict on the hearing card, and THE PARTY's batched suggestion after the advance offers the mark (CHAIR-NOTES item 3, zero-click marks). This volume mints and stores no party record. [CURED 2026-10-18 (f
